y strict. I can put the constraint info in matrix_tables (Table 5) description and/or footnotes.\n\nAlternatively add \"notes\" in the matrix_table entry. The schema for matrix_tables: name, columns, rows, description, footnotes[]. I'll put the flow-rate choice note into description and footnotes of Table 5 entry.\n\nLet me draft the note text: \"The flow rates Q1, Q2, Q3 and Q4 can be freely chosen as long as: values Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 are selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013; values for Q1 and Q2 are minimum values and the ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6; values for Q3 and Q4 are maximum values and the ratio Q4/Q3 = 1.25; the ratio Q3/Q1 is at least 40.\"\n\nfootnotes[]: maybe extract as footnotes with markers? There are no markers. Keep in description.\n\ntype_level characteristics:\n- ratio_q2_q1: 1.6 (from note) — but it's a constraint \"ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6\". Include as {value: 1.6}.\n- ratio_q4_q3: 1.25\n- minimum_ratio_q3_q1: {value: 40}\n\nThese are general characteristics/constraints. I'll include them as type_level. Value objects: {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}.\n\nWait, per rule 2, every characteristic value must be object with shape {value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers}. The example shows only some keys. I'll include unit_symbol and unit_id (null) consistently. footnote_markers only when present.\n\nNow model_level value objects: {\"model\": \"DN40 class 1\", \"value\": 0.32, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\"}? The R137 example: {\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5} — unit at attribute level (\"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\" on the attribute). The schema: model_level[]: {attribute, unit, values[]: {model, value, footnote_markers[]}}. So unit is at the attribute level: use \"unit_symbol\" (example uses \"unit_symbol\" in one place and \"unit\" in schema; the R137 example uses \"unit_symbol\"). I'll use \"unit_symbol\".\n\nSo:\n```json\n{\"attribute\": \"minimum_flow_q1\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"DN40 class 1